## Context

Discovered while verifying 0673 from a fresh clone at commit 680da23c. All 11
Quarto documents render to Markdown, and the data paper compiles to PDF, but
the corpus-report PDF fails because `deliverables/_shared/figures/fig_dag.png`
is absent from Git. A scan of Quarto documents and their include closure found
40 distinct referenced PNG figures that are gitignored and absent in the fresh
clone. The affected documents are corpus-report (5), multilayer (11),
slides-eshet (1), technical-report (35), and zoo (35); lists overlap.

These figures are a separate Phase-2 output class from the Markdown tables
fixed by 0673. They need their own handoff policy and guard. The PDF sweep's
first concrete failure is in corpus-report; the static scan shows the wider
exposure without claiming every document has been PDF-rendered.

## Actions

1. Decide which figure outputs must be committed for a clean Phase-3 render,
   or revise the writing workpackage contract explicitly if it requires a
   prebuilt figure bundle.
2. Apply the policy to every submission deliverable and the slide decks.
3. Extend the artifact guard to catch a newly referenced missing figure.

## Exit criteria

- [ ] Every submission deliverable compiles from a fresh worktree with no
      Phase-2 run or manual artifact copying.
- [ ] A missing referenced figure fails an automated test before Quarto runs.
